{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJuu38sEV2Xa5a7mCjPu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `matplotlib.__version_info__`, a named tuple shaped like `sys.version_info` with fields `(major, minor, micro, releaselevel, serial)`. Plain tuple comparisons now work, e.g. `matplotlib.__version_info__ >= (3, 4)`. The 4 tests in `test_matplotlib.py` pass, and a spot-check of the parser gave the expected results:\n\n| Version string | `__version_info__` |\n|---|---|\n| `3.5.0` | `(3, 5, 0, 'final', 0)` |\n| `3.5.0rc2` | `(3, 5, 0, 'candidate', 2)` |\n| `3.5.0b1` | `(3, 5, 0, 'beta', 1)` |\n| `3.5.0.dev820+g…` | `(3, 5, 0, 'alpha', 820)` |\n| `3.5.0.post820+g…` | `(3, 5, 1, 'alpha', 820)` |\n\nThe changes are all in `lib/matplotlib/__init__.py`:\n- **New parser:** `_parse_to_version_info()` turns a version string into the tuple, using `packaging`, which the module already imports.\n- **Refactor:** the existing version lookup moved unchanged into a helper, `_get_version()`.\n- **Lazy loading:** `__version__` and `__version_info__` are both computed on first access and cached, as `__version__` already was.\n\nTwo things to know:\n- **Post-release builds round the patch number up:** a `.post` build (what an untagged git checkout produces) is treated as an alpha of the next patch release. That's why `3.5.0.post820` maps to `(3, 5, 1, 'alpha', 820)`. A `.dev` build, by contrast, keeps its own patch number because it comes before that release.\n- **This checkout reports 0.0.1:** the repo has no release tags, so here `__version__` is `0.0.post1+ga47d2c2…` and `__version_info__` comes out as `(0, 0, 1, 'alpha', 1)`. That's expected for this repo and doesn't indicate a bug.\n\nI also added a short \"what's new\" note at `doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":23553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7217fde4-a723-4821-a547-eda4b2c8af38","uuid":"77e71606-d8f6-467c-9976-d2c800b8d397","timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:28:15.025Z","request_id":"req_011ChJuu2yT8poiSJNESZAeD"}
